course: dictionary
lesson: 15086
title: Roadway and pavement
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A roadway is the part of a road that cars and other vehicles drive on. «Cars drive on the roadway, and people walk on the pavement.» The roadway is for vehicles, and the pavement, which is called the sidewalk in some places, is for people on foot.
explain: Roadway can also mean a road in general, especially a main road. «The roadway was blocked by a fallen tree.» The clue is blocked: cars could not get past, so roadway must mean the road itself.
explain: To check a meaning, swap it into the sentence. «Stay on the pavement and cross the roadway only at a zebra crossing.» Roadway fits here because you cross the place where cars drive, and that is why you must be careful.
fact: Roadway means the part of a road that vehicles drive on.
fact: The pavement, or sidewalk, is the part of the road for people walking.
fact: Roadway can also mean a main road in general.
fact: Pupils should stay on the pavement and cross the roadway only at safe places, like zebra crossings.
fact: A «roadway closed» sign means cars cannot pass.
exercise: «Cars drive on the roadway, and people walk on the pavement.» Which part is for cars? | The pavement | The garden | The bench | *The roadway
exercise: «The roadway was flooded after the storm.» What does flooded tell you about the roadway? | *It was covered with water | It was painted bright red | It was turned into a park | It was full of people dancing
exercise: Where should you cross the roadway? | *At a safe place, like a zebra crossing | Running across in the middle of the road | Under a parked car | Anywhere you like, quickly
test: «The roadway was blocked by a fallen tree.» What does roadway mean here? | The pavement for walking | *The road itself, especially a main road | A kind of tree | A zebra crossing
test: Where should you walk when there is a roadway beside you? | Walk on the roadway with the cars | *Walk on the pavement | Run across the roadway | Sit down on the roadway
exam: Ella says roadway and pavement mean the same thing. Which is correct? | Neither word is used about roads | They are the same, and both are for cars | *Roadway is where cars drive, and pavement is for people walking | Pavement is where cars drive, and roadway is for walking
